  "scope": {
    "runtime": "The clerk runs began immediately after its Yes/No choice. Each purchase used the previous balances. Party, cash, Coin Case and zero coins were set up initially. The normal prize menu, its confirmation, delivery and debit ran on each game build.",
    "linked_roms": "All three rows at each of three prize windows were read from each stock ROM with its corresponding symbol file. Prices use two packed-decimal bytes.",
    "model": "Each integer from 0 through 9999 is a possible starting balance. Assume the player has a Coin Case and enough money. Only buy coins from the clerk until the price is affordable or another purchase is refused. An already affordable price counts. For Red Porygon, enough coins means exactly 9999.",
    "earlier_clerk_boundaries": "See stock_and_prototype_results.coins and coins-edited in scope-sweep-checks.json for the original 10 single-attempt cases per color and build. Those tests ended at the receipt or refusal."
